  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 125 PM EDT Tue Oct 27 2026\n\nSurface high pressure with ridging aloft will keep dry and mild \nconditions in place across the forecast area through the end of \nthe week, with afternoon temperatures likely 5-7 degrees above \nnormal. \n\nOn Friday a shortwave will eject out of the southern Rockies and\ninto the plains, and eventually further east into the midwest or\nthe Ohio valley depending on what model source you look at.\nLocally, downstream ridging will be amplified ahead of this \nshortwave and will keep us dry Friday into Saturday. Current NBM \nguidance brings some slight chances into the southern plateau by \nSat afternoon and evening, but I would think this will be removed\nin coming forecasts as dry conditions are the norm area wide both\nin a majority of deterministic model runs and the AI versions of \nthe ECMWF and GFS. Interestingly enough though, H85 winds do begin\nto increase on Sat ahead of that shortwave. While it doesn't look\nlike it will need wind headlines at the moment, we could be \nlooking at some gusty winds in those downslope wind prone areas.\n\nThe aforementioned trough moves through the region on Sunday,\nleading to better chances for widespread rainfall, though rainfall\namounts do appear light overall. We'll likely see dry conditions\nand above normal temperatures heading into early next week, with \nanother system moving into the region beyond the forecast period.",
